{"from": "observation:lunar-eclipse-4-bce-03-13", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-02-19-herod-died", "grade": "D", "note": "Partial lunar eclipse of 13 March 4 BCE (NASA 04813), the standard candidate (Schurer) for the eclipse Josephus places between Herod's execution of Matthias's followers and his death; the identification is disputed - opponents argue the time to Passover is too short, and Steinmann dates the death to 1 BCE instead."}
{"from": "observation:lunar-eclipse-1-bce-01-10", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-02-19-herod-died", "grade": "D", "note": "Total lunar eclipse of 10 January 1 BCE (NASA 04821); Wikipedia (Herod the Great) reports a 1 BCE chronology (Steinmann) taking Josephus's fast day, eclipse and Passover sequence at face value. The identification of Josephus's eclipse is disputed against the 4 BCE candidate, so grade D."}
